### Requests you can run from IntelliJ IDEA or VS Code (REST Client extension).
### Start the app first, e.g. with the "local" profile (see README).

@base = http://localhost:8080

### List applications (newest first)
GET {{base}}/api/applications

### Filter by status and search company/role
GET {{base}}/api/applications?status=APPLIED&q=java&sort=company,asc

### Create
POST {{base}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "company": "Example Corp",
  "role": "Junior Java Developer",
  "location": "Remote",
  "jobUrl": "https://example.com/careers/123",
  "source": "LinkedIn",
  "status": "APPLIED",
  "nextFollowUpOn": "2026-12-01"
}

### Get one
GET {{base}}/api/applications/1

### Move to the next status
POST {{base}}/api/applications/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "OFFER",
  "note": "Verbal offer after final round"
}

### Timeline of status changes
GET {{base}}/api/applications/1/history

### Follow-ups due today or earlier
GET {{base}}/api/applications/follow-ups

### Job search stats
GET {{base}}/api/stats

### Delete
DELETE {{base}}/api/applications/4
